    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A small republic built a trading empire across four continents through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">VOC</a> and the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Company.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">VOC</a>'s permanent capital and tradable shares created a model of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joint-stock-company">joint-stock company</a> still recognisable today.</li><li>Weakened by wars with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">VOC</a> was dissolved in 1799; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence">Indonesian independence</a> in 1949 ended its Asian empire.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-grotius">Hugo Grotius</a> wrote <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mare-liberum">Mare Liberum</a> (1609) in defence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">VOC</a>, and it became a founding text of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-law">international law</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

